<h1>Pick Feature Points</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Registration <i style="font-weight:bold;">&gt; <span class="Path" lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold; font-style:normal;"><b><span class="Path">Pick Feature Points</span></b></span></i>.</b></span></p>
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Pick Feature Points</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command activates capturing of feature points, which is the first step of the registration process.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Open the two entities surfaces in separate windows. Use</span> <span class="Path">Window &gt; Tile Vertically</span> <span lang="EN-GB">or</span> <span class="Path">Windows &gt; Tile Horizontally</span> <span lang="EN-GB">to display the windows side by side with the same orientation.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Call the command</span> <span class="Command">Pick Feature Points</span> <span lang="EN-GB">and select the corresponding points in both windows.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="Commands_files/image284.gif" width="32px" height="32px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt="">&#160;&#160;&#160; Mouse pointers in</span> <span class="Mode">Pick Feature Points</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB">Pick points:</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Click on a point in one window and the corresponding point in the other. Pick as many points as necessary (at least three), defining synonymously both surfaces. The picked points are temporary created and will not appear as entities in the Entities Tab. Each point is labeled according to its order of creation.</span></p>
<p class="Warning"><span lang="EN-GB">Avoid defining points in regular form as parallelepiped or a pyramid. This may lead to unwanted rotation or/and translation of the surfaces. If such thing happens, you need to choose one more point.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Ensure the correspondence of the points to be as much as possible. Use distinguished marks on the surfaces such as corners for example.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Delete feature points</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="Registration_files/image16.gif" width="308px" height="178px" border="0" class="img_whs5" alt=""></span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">If you want to delete a point right-click on it and choose</span> <span class="Command">Delete Feature Point</span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-style:italic;"><i>.</i></span></p>
<p><span class="Command">Delete all</span> will delete all picked points in this document.</p>
